# The shallow and cavern bands: the first real underground, 8..210 cells below
# the local surface row. Authoring rules are in content/mobs/surface.mob and the
# full rationale in tools/contentc/schema/mob.ts.
#
# HABITAT MODEL. A creature is eligible at a candidate cell when its depth band
# matches, the depth is inside any explicit minDepth/maxDepth window, the
# dominant biome is in its list (absent = anywhere), and any extra predicate
# (needsLava) holds. Eligible defs are then picked by weight — population
# composition follows the terrain, and there is no per-biome spawn table to keep
# in sync with the world generator.
#
# ---- ADDRESSING THE UNDERGROUND LAYERS -------------------------------------
# `biomes` names a SURFACE biome, and the five underground layers in
# src/sim/biomes.ts (caverns, grottos, magma, geode, fungal) are chosen from
# their own climate field at their own frequency — so a Desert can sit on top of
# flooded grottos and nothing in a `biomes` list can express "down there".
# Until the spawn picker learns about layers, a creature is fitted to one by the
# predicates that already exist and that the layer's own definition implies:
#
#   magma    `needsLava` + `lavaImmune` — the layer whose pocket liquid IS lava
#   grottos  a depth window in the flooded band, `gravityScale 0` to swim it
#   geode    a deep window, and immunities that match a body made of crystal
#   fungal   a deep window and `immune poison acid` — the layer pools acid
#
# That is a fit, not a gate: a slagworm can in principle surface in a dry deep
# tunnel that happens to have lava nearby. Making it exact needs a `layers`
# field on this schema AND a read of the layer id in the spawner, which is one
# change across two owners rather than one, and is called out as such rather
# than half-built here.

# --- Slime ------------------------------------------------------------------
# A wobbling blob that hops. No biome list: it is the one creature that belongs
# everywhere underground, and the band pair (not the biome) is what places it.
# The short beat makes it a rhythm to time rather than a chase to outrun.
@mob slime
name          Slime
brain         hopper
maxHealth     20
contactDamage 10
bodyCellsW    3
bodyCellsH    2
speed         190
jumpSpeed     640
aggroPx       145
aggroYPx      70
beat          1.05
blood         #49b077
xp            5
value         2
drops         item=slime_gel count=1..2
bands         shallow cavern
weight        20

# A blob has no limbs, so every frame is a change of VOLUME: the idle squashes
# and rises, and the air pose compresses at launch and stretches at the apex.
# Two extra palette tones (a dark base, a surface sheen) give it a bottom and a
# top, which is the only thing that stopped the old two-frame version reading as
# a green rectangle blinking.
art.cellsW 3
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #1e4a34 #2c6f4a #49b077 #a8f0c4
art.fps    6
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=3.1 blinkFor=0.16 |
  .4.
  232

  ...
  333

  434
  333
art.seq  state=move mode=loop |
  ...
  333

  .4.
  232

  .3.
  333
art.seq  state=air mode=once fps=9 |
  .4.
  .3.

  434
  333

# --- Cave bat ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The only species eligible in every band, so its weight is held down to stop
# caves reading as nothing but bats. Nocturnal, which at the surface multiplies
# its weight by darkness — underground the multiplier is 1, because a cave is
# dark at noon.
@mob bat
name          Cave Bat
brain         flyer
maxHealth     10
contactDamage 6
attackCooldown 0.7
bodyCellsW    3
bodyCellsH    2
speed         200
chaseSpeed    360
gravityScale  0
aggroPx       170
aggroYPx      130
beat          0.9
blood         #4a3d5c
xp            3
drops         item=bat_wing count=1 chance=40%
bands         surface shallow cavern deep
nocturnal     yes
weight        12

# A FOUR-frame wingbeat, which is the whole reason this redraw exists: the old
# two-frame version was up/down with nothing between, so at 14fps it strobed.
# Up, mid, down, mid gives the beat a direction, and the mid frames use the
# darker wing tone so the wing reads as edge-on rather than as half-erased.
# `air` is the dive: wings gone entirely, which is unmistakable against a pose
# whose whole identity is wings.
art.cellsW 3
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #1a1424 #2a2233 #4a3d5c #ff9a6b
art.fps    14
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=3.6 blinkFor=0.12 |
  3.3
  .4.

  ...
  343

  3.3
  .2.
art.seq  state=move mode=loop |
  3.3
  .4.

  2.2
  343

  ...
  343

  2.2
  343
art.seq  state=air mode=hold |
  ...
  343

# --- Stoneback --------------------------------------------------------------
# The armour test. 8 flat reduction against a PUNCH_DAMAGE of 5 means bare fists
# do the floored minimum of 1 per swing — it is not unkillable, it is a creature
# that tells you to go and find a pick. Slow, short-sighted and non-committal
# (no jumpSpeed, so it will not follow you off a ledge); the threat is entirely
# that it is standing between you and the ore.
@mob stoneback
name          Stoneback
brain         walker
maxHealth     55
contactDamage 14
attackCooldown 1.2
armor         8
immune        impact
bodyCellsW    4
bodyCellsH    3
speed         80
chaseSpeed    130
aggroPx       110
aggroYPx      55
beat          3.2
blood         #6e6e6e
xp            18
value         10
drops         item=stone_chunk count=2..4
drops         item=iron_ore count=1..2 chance=45%
drops         item=gem count=1 chance=8%
bands         cavern deep
weight        9

# Twelve cells and four of them are legs, so this is the one creature with room
# for a real quadruped gait: four distinct footfall patterns on row 2 — planted,
# front pair, passing, rear pair — under a shell that never moves. A heavy thing
# should look like its mass is being carried, and the way to say that at this
# grain is that the top two thirds are completely still.
art.cellsW 4
art.cellsH 3
art.pal    . #262626 #3a3a3a #6e6e6e #8f8f8f #b8b8b8
art.fps    4
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=5.5 blinkFor=0.2 |
  .44.
  3333
  1..1

  .44.
  3223
  .11.

  .54.
  3333
  1..1
art.seq  state=move mode=phase |
  .44.
  3333
  1..1

  .44.
  3333
  .1.1

  .44.
  3333
  .11.

  .44.
  3333
  1.1.
art.seq  state=air mode=hold |
  .44.
  3333
  ....

# --- Cinder moth ------------------------------------------------------------
# A flyer for the volcanic surface and the hot shallows: it glows, it is immune
# to fire (it nests in it), and it spits embers rather than closing, so it is
# the first creature that punishes you for standing on open ground. Nocturnal,
# because a moth you can see coming is not a moth.
@mob cinder_moth
name          Cinder Moth
brain         flyer
maxHealth     12
contactDamage 5
attackCooldown 0.8
bodyCellsW    3
bodyCellsH    2
speed         180
chaseSpeed    300
gravityScale  0
aggroPx       185
aggroYPx      120
beat          1.1
glow          0.35
immune        fire
blood         #ff7a2c
ranged.projectile ember
ranged.cooldown   2.2
ranged.range      190
ranged.damage     7
xp            8
value         4
drops         item=ash_pile count=1..2
drops         item=moth_dust count=1 chance=30%
bands         surface shallow cavern
biomes        volcanic desert savanna
nocturnal     yes
weight        11

# The interrupt frame is the fifth palette entry and nothing else in the sprite
# ever uses it: the wings go white-hot for a tenth of a second, which is the
# tell that an ember is coming. That is the single most useful thing `ambient`
# bought this file — a ranged attacker that telegraphs, without a line of code.
art.cellsW 3
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #3a1408 #4a1e10 #ff7a2c #ffd68a #fff2c8
art.fps    13
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=2.4 blinkFor=0.1 |
  4.4
  .3.

  2.2
  232

  5.5
  .3.
art.seq  state=move mode=loop |
  4.4
  .3.

  2.2
  232

  ...
  434

  2.2
  232
art.seq  state=air mode=hold |
  ...
  434

# --- Skeleton ---------------------------------------------------------------
# NEW, and overdue: the README's whole first sentence about combat is "Defeat
# army of skeletons", and there were none. Deliberately built as a DARK MIRROR
# OF THE PLAYER — same 2x3 body, same head/torso/legs rows, same four-frame run
# cadence — because that is what makes an army of them read as an army rather
# than as another cave animal. It is a traveler that did not get back out.
#
# Packs of two to four, each individually weaker than a stoneback, is the
# difference between the two encounters: the stoneback asks whether your pick is
# good enough, the skeletons ask whether you picked the right corridor.
#
# `stone` is the projectile because the enum is closed (MobSystem.ts owns what a
# projectile does), and of the four available it is the only one that can be
# read as a thrown bone. Immune to poison for the obvious reason.
@mob skeleton
name          Skeleton
brain         walker
maxHealth     24
contactDamage 11
attackCooldown 0.9
armor         1
immune        poison
bodyCellsW    2
bodyCellsH    3
speed         120
chaseSpeed    210
jumpSpeed     500
aggroPx       200
aggroYPx      90
beat          2
blood         #e4dcc4
ranged.projectile stone
ranged.cooldown   2.1
ranged.range      200
ranged.damage     8
xp            10
value         5
# Bone is an arrow shaft (content/items/creatures.item), so the thing shooting
# at you in the dark is also what restocks your quiver. The stray arrows are the
# ones it did not get to throw.
drops         item=bone count=1..3
drops         item=arrow count=1..3 chance=30%
bands         cavern deep
packSize      2..4
weight        15

art.cellsW 2
art.cellsH 3
art.pal    . #6e6a5c #b8b098 #e4dcc4 #ff5a4a
art.fps    8
# The eye kindling red is the interrupt, and it is the same event as the
# sentinel's optic: on the two creatures in the game that shoot at you, the
# ambient tell means "it has seen you".
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=2.9 blinkFor=0.14 |
  .3
  22
  11

  .3
  21
  11

  .4
  22
  11
art.seq  state=move mode=phase |
  .3
  22
  1.

  .3
  22
  11

  .3
  22
  .1

  .3
  22
  11
art.seq  state=air mode=once fps=10 |
  .3
  22
  .1

  .3
  23
  ..

# --- Glimmerback ------------------------------------------------------------
# NEW. The Geode Hollows creature. That layer is the one with `veinRich` and
# `veinCommon` both set to crystal and a caveScale of 0.85 — tight, glittering,
# and the richest thing in the game to mine — and until now it had nobody living
# in it, so the reward was free.
#
# It is built as a TOLL rather than as a threat: armour 6 and immunity to impact
# mean punching it is pointless and even a copper pick's owner is trading a real
# amount of time, but it is slow (90), short-sighted (120px) and cannot jump, so
# it can simply be walked around. The choice it poses is "is this seam worth the
# fight", which is the only interesting question a guard can ask.
@mob glimmerback
name          Glimmerback
brain         walker
maxHealth     34
contactDamage 12
attackCooldown 1.1
armor         6
immune        ice impact
bodyCellsW    3
bodyCellsH    2
speed         90
chaseSpeed    140
aggroPx       120
aggroYPx      50
beat          2.8
glow          0.4
blood         #b48aff
xp            20
value         14
drops         item=crystal_shard count=2..4
drops         item=gem count=1 chance=30%
bands         cavern deep
minDepth      120
weight        8

# Crystal on top, animal underneath. The spine is the only part that changes in
# the idle and the body is the only part that changes in the walk, so the two
# poses never compete — and `glow 0.4` means the spine survives the darkness
# mask, which is what makes one of these visible across an unlit geode chamber.
art.cellsW 3
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #2e2450 #5a4a92 #a888e8 #e8d8ff #ffffff
art.fps    5
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=3.8 blinkFor=0.16 |
  .4.
  323

  .3.
  323

  454
  323
art.seq  state=move mode=phase |
  .4.
  123

  .4.
  323

  .4.
  321

  .4.
  323
art.seq  state=air mode=hold |
  .4.
  .3.

# --- Gulper -----------------------------------------------------------------
# NEW. The Flooded Grottos creature. That layer has caveScale 1.35 and a
# NEGATIVE pocketBias, which is the generator being told to actually flood it —
# so it is the one place underground that is mostly liquid, and it was empty.
#
# `flyer` with `gravityScale 0` is how a swimmer is spelled with the brains that
# exist: it holds a height, drifts, and closes fast. The depth window (20..220)
# is what keeps it in the flooded band instead of turning up in a dry surface
# cave, and it is the one creature here with no armour at all — it is fast and
# it hits hard and it dies immediately, which is the right shape for something
# that ambushes you while you are swimming and cannot swing properly.
@mob gulper
name          Gulper
brain         flyer
maxHealth     22
contactDamage 13
attackCooldown 0.8
bodyCellsW    4
bodyCellsH    2
speed         130
chaseSpeed    250
gravityScale  0
aggroPx       175
aggroYPx      110
beat          1.4
blood         #6fb0c0
xp            9
value         5
drops         item=worm_hide count=1..2
drops         item=slime_gel count=1 chance=35%
bands         shallow cavern
minDepth      20
maxDepth      220
weight        10

# The dorsal fin is a single lit pixel that TRAVELS head to tail across the four
# move frames while the body tones alternate underneath it. That is an
# undulation rather than a flap, and it is what distinguishes a swimmer from the
# bat at a glance even though both are flyers holding a height. The maw (5)
# appears on the idle interrupt and on the lunge, nowhere else.
art.cellsW 4
art.cellsH 2
art.pal    . #1e4450 #3f7f8c #6fb0c0 #bfeaf2 #ff8a6b
art.fps    9
art.seq  state=idle mode=ambient blinkEvery=3.2 blinkFor=0.14 |
  .44.
  2332

  .34.
  2332

  .44.
  2335
art.seq  state=move mode=loop |
  4...
  2332

  .4..
  3223

  ..4.
  2332

  ...4
  3223
art.seq  state=air mode=hold |
  .44.
  2335
